# Backend Quality Standards

- Use async end-to-end for I/O paths; avoid blocking calls in request flow.
- Add explicit type hints for public functions and service/repository interfaces.
- Implement tests first for new behavior (endpoint contract + service unit tests).
- Every feature PR must include passing tests for happy path and expected failures.
- Never commit IDE files, temporary artifacts, local databases, or environment secrets.
- Map upstream failures to explicit API error codes; avoid opaque generic 500 payloads.
